  "rationale": "The representative prefix ends in a noun in an opening title-like phrase, but the model assigns nearly all its mass to punctuation rather than the paragraph break that follows these opening nominal phrases throughout the batch documents. Add a compositional rule for the observed opening shapes, without conditioning on a particular name or noun. The batch also includes “for” after “all” and “is” after “That”; the existing “is” rule covers “This” but not “That.” These targeted lexical-context rules address those observations while leaving other continuations available. A nominal phrase may sometimes continue as a sentence rather than a heading, and other words after “all” or “That” can be valid, so the rules add evidence rather than assert exclusivity. The replay gate has not been evaluated for this patch.",
